# XSH iconv()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The standard names no code set: every test probes a short list of
# familiar names (UTF-8, US-ASCII, ISO-8859-1 and their usual spellings)
# and is UNRESOLVED when none opens. Text that converts identically is
# limited to the portable characters, whose single byte values XBD fixes;
# the tests that need an invalid byte, an incomplete character or a
# character with no counterpart use UTF-8 as the input code set and
# US-ASCII (or ISO-8859-1) as the target, with the usual byte values of
# those code sets. Output bytes for characters without an identical
# counterpart are not checked.

assertion  XSH.iconv.001
anchor     functions/iconv.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iconv.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1992
says       Converting portable-character text between two ASCII-compatible
           code sets gives the same bytes, returns 0, leaves inbytesleft 0,
           moves inbuf past the input, advances outbuf by the bytes written
           and lowers outbytesleft by the same amount.
test       t/001-portable-identical.c

assertion  XSH.iconv.002
anchor     functions/iconv.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iconv.html#ERRORS
class      required
since      1992
says       When the output buffer is too small, iconv() returns -1 with
           E2BIG after converting what fits (three of six single-byte
           characters), leaving inbuf, inbytesleft, outbuf and outbytesleft
           describing exactly that; a further call on the remaining input
           with a larger buffer finishes the text; a buffer of exactly the
           needed size is enough.
test       t/002-e2big-resume.c

assertion  XSH.iconv.003
anchor     functions/iconv.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iconv.html#ERRORS
class      required
since      1992
says       When the next input character needs more output bytes than are
           left (one byte left, a two-byte result), conversion stops just
           before that character: -1 with E2BIG, the characters before it
           converted, inbuf and inbytesleft pointing at it.
test       t/003-e2big-whole-character.c

assertion  XSH.iconv.004
anchor     functions/iconv.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iconv.html#ERRORS
class      required
since      1992
says       An input byte that is not valid in the input code set (0xFF in
           UTF-8) stops conversion with -1 and EILSEQ after the previous
           converted character; inbuf points at the byte and inbytesleft
           counts it and the rest.
test       t/004-eilseq.c

assertion  XSH.iconv.005
anchor     functions/iconv.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iconv.html#ERRORS
class      required
since      1992
says       An incomplete character at the end of the input (the first byte
           of a two-byte UTF-8 character) stops conversion with -1 and
           EINVAL after the previous converted character; inbuf points at
           the incomplete character.
test       t/005-einval.c

assertion  XSH.iconv.006
anchor     functions/iconv.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iconv.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2024
says       With the //IGNORE suffix on the target name, an invalid input byte
           that is followed by a valid character is discarded without error:
           the return value is not -1, inbytesleft is 0 and the output holds
           the valid characters on both sides.
note       The return value for the discarded bytes is not checked (Q-129).
test       t/006-ignore-invalid.c

assertion  XSH.iconv.007
anchor     functions/iconv.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iconv_open.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       With //NON_IDENTICAL_DISCARD, a valid character that has no
           identical counterpart in the target code set is dropped from the
           output but counted: the return value is 1, inbytesleft 0 and the
           output holds the characters on both sides.
test       t/007-non-identical-discard.c

assertion  XSH.iconv.008
anchor     functions/iconv.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iconv_open.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       With //IGNORE, a valid character with no identical counterpart is
           also dropped from the output and counted: the return value is 1,
           inbytesleft 0 and the output holds the characters on both sides.
test       t/008-ignore-non-identical.c

assertion  XSH.iconv.009
anchor     functions/iconv.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iconv_open.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2024
says       With //TRANSLIT, a valid character with no identical counterpart
           counts once in the return value however many characters replace
           it (1 here), whether or not a transliteration exists; inbytesleft
           is 0 and the output starts and ends with the characters around it.
test       t/009-translit-count.c

assertion  XSH.iconv.010
anchor     functions/iconv.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/iconv.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2024
says       With no suffix, a valid character with no identical counterpart is
           converted in an implementation-defined way and counted: the call
           does not fail, returns 1, leaves inbytesleft 0 and the output
           starts and ends with the characters around it.
note       Systems that report EILSEQ for such a character do not follow the
           stated behaviour.
test       t/010-no-suffix-counted.c

assertion  XSH.iconv.011
anchor     functions/iconv.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       A call with a null inbuf, and a call with inbuf pointing to a null
           pointer (with a null outbuf or with an output buffer) is not an
           error, and the descriptor still converts afterwards.
test       t/011-reset-forms.c

assertion  XSH.iconv.012
anchor     functions/iconv.html#APPLICATION USAGE
class      required
since      1992
says       A zero byte inside the input is an ordinary character: three bytes
           "a", NUL, "b" give three output bytes with the NUL kept and
           inbytesleft 0.
test       t/012-nul-is-data.c
